#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-07.png", width: 115.5pt), 374pt, 83.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 81.72pt, "The proposed metrics - formulated in detail in the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 95.52pt, "preceding sections - are evaluated for their suitability ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 109.32pt, "using the following procedure. Each image sequence is ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 123.12pt, "treated as an index-ordered set of frames, and the metric ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 136.92pt, "value is computed for every image index. This results a ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 150.72pt, "one-dimensional metric curve that represents the evolution ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 164.52pt, "of the structural characteristics captured by the metric. In ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 178.32pt, "this context, the notion of suitability refers to how well the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 192.12pt, "resulting metric curve reflects the presence, persistence, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 205.92pt, "and evolution of defect-related structural patterns within ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 219.72pt, "the sequence. For comparative assessment, the signal-to-")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 233.52pt, "noise ratio (SNR) and the Tanimoto criterion are employed ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 247.32pt, "as reference metrics, allowing the proposed measures to be ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 261.12pt, "evaluated against established indicators of image quality ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 274.92pt, "and structural relevance. The calculation of the SNR, as ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 288.72pt, "per Equation (4), for each integrated defect in the plate ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 302.52pt, "illustrated in Figure 2, the reference region was selected as ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 316.32pt, "follows. A region of interest (ROI) containing the defect ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 330.12pt, "was initially specified from the entire dataset. Within this ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 343.92pt, "ROI, the area surrounding the defect was designated as the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 357.72pt, "reference region (Figure 4), thereby providing a basis for calculating the SNR relative to the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 371.52pt, "defect. The determination of the defect region and the subsequent calculation of the Tanimoto ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 385.32pt, "criterion are achieved through the implementation of the contour-search algorithm, as outlined ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 399.12pt, "in [9]. This method has demonstrated an enhanced performance in comparison to conventional ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 412.92pt, "approaches, particularly in the context of automated processing of IRT datasets [9]. In response ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 426.72pt, "to the potential impact of factors such as non-uniform heating during the experiment on both ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 440.52pt, "the ROI and the computed metrics - particularly the two reference metrics, SNR and TC - a ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 454.32pt, "spatial filter is applied to each image during the preprocessing phase. A detailed description of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 468.12pt, "the filter, including its advantages and limitations, is provided and discussed in [8]. The filter's ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 481.92pt, "operation involves the subtraction of an empirically interpolated image, which is generated ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 495.72pt, "according to the formula (9), from the original image. This process reduces gradual intensity ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 509.52pt, "variations and enhances the contrast of local defect-related features. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 575.16pt, "where")
