  #line-at(88.8pt, 123.12pt, "During the experiments, a xenon lamp was used to thermally excite the entire CFRP plate, ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 136.92pt, "enabling full-field thermographic acquisition of the specimen surface. Regions of interest ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 150.72pt, "(ROIs) were then extracted from the recorded thermograms and processed as image sequences. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 164.52pt, "During pre-processing, saturated regions [10] as well as frames affected by the afterglow effect ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 178.32pt, "[34] were excluded from further analysis. The thermographic images had a pixel size of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 192.12pt, "approximately 0.3 mm, resulting in ROI dimensions of 118 × 118 pixels. Initially, the proposed ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 205.92pt, "evaluation methodology described in Section 3.2.1 was applied to the cropped ROI thermogram ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 219.72pt, "sequences. To reduce computational time, the analysis was limited to the first 10 seconds of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 233.52pt, "each thermogram sequence. Two representative results corresponding to the near-surface and ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 247.32pt, "deepest defect regions, denoted as ROI 1 and ROI 6, respectively, are presented in Figure 9. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 261.12pt, "The analysis of the remaining ROIs is provided in Appendix A.   ")
  #line-at(106.201pt, 274.92pt, "A comparative analysis between the three proposed metrics (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(403.92pt, 274.92pt, "HI / REA / TVE")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(481.2pt, 274.92pt, ") and the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 288.72pt, "reference metrics (SNR / TC) reveals that they generally exhibit qualitatively similar behaviors. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 302.52pt, "In regions of high defect detectability - corresponding to indices with pronounced contrast - ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 316.32pt, "they display well-defined global or local maxima, indicating clear sensitivity to defect areas. ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 330.12pt, "Conversely, in regions of low defect detectability at higher indices, all proposed metrics ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 343.92pt, "converge towards a nearly constant value, reflecting stable baseline behavior. Across all ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 357.72pt, "metrics, with the exception of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(217.44pt, 357.72pt, "TVE")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(238.8pt, 357.72pt, ", noise levels are relatively high and largely independent of ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 371.52pt, "the ROI. In order to enhance visual clarity and facilitate comparison, high-frequency ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 385.32pt, "components were suppressed using a band-pass filter, and filtered signals are indicated with ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 399.12pt, "dashed lines in the figures. The behavior of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
