#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12.283pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.799pt, 81.72pt, "static window strategies offer computational efficiency, their inherent rigidity limits their ")
  #line-at(70.799pt, 95.519pt, "general applicability. Conversely, the randomized window selection approach, in ")
  #line-at(70.799pt, 109.318pt, "combination with statistically justified number of samples planning, offers a flexible and ")
  #line-at(70.799pt, 123.117pt, "robust alternative. The results demonstrate that stable and representative outcomes can ")
  #line-at(70.799pt, 136.922pt, "often be achieved with a reduced number of window samples, indicating significant ")
  #line-at(70.799pt, 150.72pt, "potential for further reductions in computational cost without compromising result quality.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.8pt, 164.52pt, "A comparison of computation times among the proposed metrics reveals that HI generally ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 179.4pt, "requires significantly less processing time compared to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(358.2pt, 179.4pt, "REA")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.16pt, 179.4pt, " and ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(409.32pt, 179.4pt, "TVE")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(430.8pt, 179.4pt, ". To illustrate, the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 194.4pt, "processing of a single ROI sequence of dimensions 118 × 118 × 1781 currently requires ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 209.28pt, "approximately 47 seconds for the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(244.44pt, 209.28pt, "HI")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(257.04pt, 209.28pt, " metric curve, depending on the available computing ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 224.16pt, "resources (see Appendix D). Nevertheless, there is considerable potential for optimization in ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 239.04pt, "future implementations, which could reduce the computation time of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(445.44pt, 239.04pt, "REA")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(467.4pt, 239.04pt, " and ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(500.04pt, 239.04pt, "TVE")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(521.4pt, 239.04pt, ". ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 253.92pt, "Furthermore, the validity of the proposed methodology was further supported through ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 268.8pt, "comparison with theoretical predictions derived from a one-dimensional N-layer analytical ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 283.68pt, "thermal model, as well as with corresponding simulations and calculation of the thermal ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 298.56pt, "diffusion length. Especially, qualitative correlation was observed between the frequency-")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 313.44pt, "dependent ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(122.88pt, 313.44pt, "HI")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(135.48pt, 313.44pt, " curves obtained from the PPT amplitude image sequences and the corresponding ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 328.32pt, "simulated contrast curves based on thermal diffusion length. The findings of both approaches ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 343.2pt, "indicated that there was close alignment of peak frequencies of approximately 0.1 Hz for all ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 358.2pt, "regions of interest (ROIs), in addition to consistent trends in peak width and slope for defects ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 373.08pt, "ranging from the surface to the depths. In addition, a comparable transition region was identified ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 387.96pt, "in both the experimental and simulated results. This region is interpreted as a blind-frequency ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 402.84pt, "or knee-point region with reduced defect detectability. These findings confirm the ability of the ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 417.72pt, "proposed metrics to identify defect-related features and to correlate with simulated physical ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 432.6pt, "contrast predictions. Overall, the results confirm that the proposed metrics and framework ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 447.48pt, "provide a robust, automated, and computationally efficient system for detecting and further ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 462.36pt, "quantifying anomalies and defects in various thermographic data sequences, with great potential ")
  #line-at(70.8pt, 477.24pt, "for extension to other materials, excitation schemes, and imaging methods. ")
]

